  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAF Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAFCO Venture Holdings Limited BVI (SAFCO Venture or the Company) is a company established to own and operate biodiesel and sustainable aviation fuel (SAF) production facilities in Pakistan. Through its subsidiary Bio Tech Energy Pte Ltd (BTE), SAFCO Venture owns and operates a 50,000 tons per annum (tpa) biodiesel manufacturing facility in Sheikhupura, Pakistan.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project is anticipated to yield significant outcomes, including: (i) environmental effects through Green House Gas (GHG) emission savings and (ii) economywide effects through the creation of 300 highly skilled jobs and the generation of export revenue for the country. Beyond the Project, IFC anticipates the investment will promote sustainability by supporting the growth of the sustainable aviation fuel sector and circular economy model to curb the growth of carbon emissions in the aviation sector.</narrative>
  </description>
